# Vercel previews — don't spam builds

Every pushed branch can trigger a Vercel preview on this repo. Agents should treat
that as a cost, not a default debugging step.

## Default: verify locally

- Prove app changes with `npm run build -w @party-tracker/app`, `npm run start -w
  @party-tracker/app`, and the relevant test suite (`npm run test:app`,
  `npm run test:functional`, etc.).
- Do **not** push a branch or open a PR for read-only investigation, Q&A, or tasks
  with no code to land.
- Do **not** push intermediate WIP commits just to "see it on Vercel" when local
  build + Playwright (or manual browser against `127.0.0.1:3000`) is enough.

## When a preview IS warranted

Push/open a PR that may hit Vercel only when the task genuinely needs deployed
behavior, for example:

- PWA install or service-worker update/reload flow
- Vercel routing, headers, or serverless/API runtime behavior
- Production-only environment variables or CDN cache headers
- A defect that does not reproduce on `npm run build && npm start`

Say in the PR why a preview is needed when you open one for that reason.

## Safety net (already on main)

`vercel.json` sets `"ignoreCommand": "bash scripts/vercel-ignore.sh"`. That skips
Vercel builds when a commit only touches docs, tests, builder tooling, or other
non-runtime paths — even if a branch exists. Agents should still avoid opening
unnecessary PR branches; the ignore step is not permission to spam pushes.
